# Evidence and reasoning invariants

Preserve:

- Change Intent ≠ Deployment ≠ realized Change;
- prospective Impact ≠ actual Impact;
- planned topology ≠ active Lineage;
- anticipated effect ≠ normative Expectation;
- planned value ≠ empirical Baseline;
- prospective reference preparation ≠ realized transition;
- Deployment attempt ≠ intent association ≠ activation ≠ intended effect realized;
- successful execution ≠ timely execution ≠ freshness ≠ data quality;
- execution-duration Observation ≠ duration violation;
- Observation ≠ Assessment;
- missing evidence ≠ observed absence;
- raw difference ≠ material Change;
- typical ≠ healthy;
- atypical ≠ degraded/defective ≠ mandatory intervention;
- Investigation ≠ source evidence/causal truth;
- Causal Claim ≠ confirmed cause;
- Impact candidate ≠ exposure ≠ downstream effect ≠ business consequence;
- safeguard proposal ≠ active safeguard;
- quarantine ≠ proof of defect;
- release ≠ proof of health;
- effective/event time ≠ recorded/knowledge time;
- correlation ≠ attribution ≠ confirmed cause.

Rules:

- Time/history is first-class with ledger-like append/supersede/correction semantics.
- Material conclusions remain traceable to provenance-bearing evidence.
- Change Intent may prepare prospective references and prospective blast-radius context without manufacturing norms, Baselines, actual Impact, or cause.
- Intent-to-Deployment association requires evidence; temporal proximity is insufficient.
- Reference transition requires sufficient realization evidence for the relevant subject/dimension/context.
- Post-transition Baseline requires sufficient comparable post-transition Observations.
- Treat execution start/completion/duration/queue/dependency-latency facts as Observations before Assessment.
- Missing timestamps/telemetry never become zero duration or missing run/output.
- Assess runtime/data evidence against the correct time-valid Expectation/Baseline.
- Ordinary variation within a Baseline must not become alert noise simply because values differ.
- Baseline atypicality is descriptive; normative violation requires Expectation.
- Analysts may investigate uncertain/material results; automatic Investigation requires explicit accepted response criteria.
- Propagation Safeguard is separate from health and cause; `propose` is not `active`.
- Activation requires explicit authority/enforcement evidence; quarantine can be precautionary.
- If no output exists, hold downstream advancement rather than inventing a quarantined object.
- Safeguard-induced delay remains valid operational evidence.
- Lineage remains typed, temporal, historical, authorization-aware, graph-compatible.
- Never infer cause from Deployment timing, Lineage, realized Change, safeguard state, or intent consistency alone.
- Multiple contributors/unresolved outcomes are valid; confirmed cause requires explicit accepted standard.
- Downstream traversal yields candidates; actual exposure/effect/consequence require separate evidence.
- Distinguish contemporaneous from retrospective knowledge when later evidence changes interpretation.
- Do not select graph database, event store, quarantine store, persistence architecture, LLM, or causal algorithm from these semantics alone.
